### Accessibility Compliance Checklist

#### ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) - US
- [ ] Website accessible to users with disabilities
- [ ] No discrimination based on disability
- [ ] Reasonable accommodations provided
- [ ] Compliance with WCAG 2.1 Level AA (recommended minimum)
- [ ] Accessibility statement published
- [ ] Contact method for accessibility concerns

#### Section 508 - US Federal
- [ ] Electronic and information technology accessible
- [ ] WCAG 2.1 Level AA compliance (required for federal)
- [ ] Section 508 standards met
- [ ] VPAT (Voluntary Product Accessibility Template) completed (if selling to government)
- [ ] Testing with assistive technologies completed

#### WCAG 2.1 Compliance
- [ ] **Perceivable**: Text alternatives, captions, sufficient contrast
- [ ] **Operable**: Keyboard accessible, no seizures, navigable
- [ ] **Understandable**: Readable, predictable, input assistance
- [ ] **Robust**: Compatible with assistive technologies
- [ ] Level AA compliance (minimum for legal protection)
- [ ] Level AAA where possible (enhanced accessibility)

#### International Accessibility Standards
- [ ] **AODA** (Canada): WCAG 2.1 Level AA compliance
- [ ] **EN 301 549** (EU): European accessibility standard
- [ ] **Regional requirements**: Check local accessibility laws

#### Accessibility Implementation
- [ ] Screen reader compatibility tested
- [ ] Keyboard navigation fully functional
- [ ] Color contrast meets WCAG standards (4.5:1 for text)
- [ ] Alternative text for all images
- [ ] Captions/transcripts for audio/video
- [ ] Form labels and error messages accessible
- [ ] Focus indicators visible
- [ ] No keyboard traps
- [ ] Accessible error handling
- [ ] Regular accessibility audits conducted

## Best Practices

1. **Privacy by Design**: Build privacy into system design
2. **Data Minimization**: Collect only what's necessary
3. **Transparency**: Clear privacy policies
4. **Security**: Encrypt sensitive data
5. **Access Controls**: Limit who can access data
6. **Audit Logging**: Track data access
7. **Regular Reviews**: Update compliance regularly
8. **Legal Consultation**: Consult legal experts for complex cases
9. **Accessibility by Design**: Build accessibility into system design from the start
10. **WCAG Compliance**: Meet WCAG 2.1 Level AA minimum (Level AAA where possible)
11. **Regular Accessibility Testing**: Test with assistive technologies regularly
12. **Accessibility Statement**: Publish clear accessibility statement with contact information

## Age-Appropriate Content

### Content Guidelines
- **Under 13**: Extra protections, parental oversight
- **13-17**: Standard protections, some autonomy
- **18+**: Full user rights

### Content Moderation
